WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.880
Iran is one of the most closed off countries in the world.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.520
But for the past year,

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.640
something seems to have been changing.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.600
In this Islamic regime,

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.880
ruled with an iron fist by the mullahs,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.920
some women are daring to defy the rules and risking their lives in the process.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.840
Across the big cities,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.960
amid hijabs and chadors,

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.920
some women are shedding their headscarves.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:31.640
This is the case for Gina.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.480
Hello!

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:36.840
A young

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.000
32-year-old Iranian woman,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.920
who has given up on more traditional clothing.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.800
A move that's considered provocative by religious leaders.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.920
I used to wear something around my neck
to go out in public or somewhere official

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.920
and I would cover my head.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.200
But now I don't even wear a scarf around my neck.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.720
I won't wear a hijab anymore.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.120
It's a way to show that I am resisting.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.880
Aren't you ashamed of doing that?

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.960
You don't have to do this.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.840
I'm begging you!
Leave her alone!

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.040
Let go of me!

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.400
Let go of me!

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.000
Some women are beaten and taken away by force.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:44.240
Grab her!
Grab her!

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.520
According to Islamic law,

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:52.200
Gina could receive up to 72 lashes for not wearing the hijab.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.040
We're not afraid anymore and we have to show
that we're protesting one way or another.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:07.440
The young generation don't want to wear the hijab
anymore, unlike the previous generation.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:18.880
To be able to dance freely.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.320
Kiss freely,

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.960
For our brothers and sisters,

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:28.400
To change this backward way of seeing things.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.240
For freedom!

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.800
For freedom!

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:55.360
In Iran there is a long list of things that are prohibited and women are on the front lines trying to reclaim more of their rights and freedoms.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:01.840
Iran is a huge country of 90 million inhabitants neighboring Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.280
Since September 2022,

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:17.080
an unprecedented rebel movement started by women has been shaking the Islamic Republic.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.160
Freedom, freedom, freedom.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.440
Freedom, freedom, freedom.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.000
It all started with the murder of Masha Jina Amini,

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:27.560
a young

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:34.160
22-year-old woman who was beaten to death by the authorities because she wasn't wearing her hijab correctly.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:40.120
A photo taken at the hospital a few hours before her death did the rounds on social media.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.360
Mashahjina Amini was a model student.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.600
She was innocence personified.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:56.800
This was a young, beautiful, provincial woman,
who came to Tehran just to visit the capital.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.760
Many Iranian women saw themselves
in her tragic story

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.360
and this crystallised the already-huge anger
that Iranians were feeling.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.160
Some women removed their hijabs as a form of protest.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.080
And some even went as far as burning them with the support of some men.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.000
A profound fury took hold of the country,

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.960
including in universities.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:19.520
Amidst the chaos,

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.920
a slogan emerged.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:21.880
Woman.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:22.760
Life.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:23.480
Freedom.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.840
In response to their protests,

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.280
the authorities fired live bullets.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.760
Allahu Akbar!

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.440
The violence was documented on social media.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:49.960
It was impossible for a Western journalist to freely investigate in Iran.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:50.760
So,

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:54.040
to tell this story of a country fighting for its rights,

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.240
we got in touch with Iranians via encrypted messaging.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.080
They're going to share their experience.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:12.320
Here, women wear the hijab in a really free and
relaxed way compared to other places in Tehran.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.400
Are you here for me?

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.240
Get out!
Go.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.960
Yes, put your clothes back on properly
and then come back.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:25.040
They're all risking their lives by denouncing the Mullah dictatorship,

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.280
a regime that uses extensive censorship.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:30.320
We must delete this part.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.960
Corrupt dignitaries who hoard the country's wealth.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:36.640
They keep it all for themselves.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:40.000
They've created a group
and share everything out between them.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.360
Determined authorities who terrorize their opponents beyond their borders.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.040
I see my dad, he's been arrested,
he's in a car, blindfolded.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.960
I'm heartbroken for him.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:55.000
An investigation into this off-limits Iran,

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.200
where young people dream of freedom within a regime that continues to suppress it.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:05.280
In Iran,

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:08.640
women can't openly talk about the oppression they suffer.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.640
But behind closed doors,

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:11.720
we meet Gina,

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.840
the young woman who refuses to wear a hijab.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.160
Hi girls, may God bless you.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.000
This afternoon,

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.480
she has gone to the beauty salon.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:31.600
Have you been there a long time?
Sit down, please.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:37.560
A small slice of freedom far from the conservative and repressive Iran that lies outside.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.960
How are you girls?
- Yeah, great!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.280
See this colour? I love it.
- Yeah, you're right, it's great!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.560
Within these walls,

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.400
women can discuss and laugh about anything at all.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:54.880
When you go out without the hijab,
you have to do your hair, put some oil in it.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:00.240
But you do it for yourself!
You're not doing if for men to look at.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.040
They're going to fall out!

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.160
When I have a headscarf on my head
and I have to wear a long tunic,

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.000
I put lipstick on to feel seen, it makes me feel alive.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:17.760
When you're in black all the time,
with gloomy clothing on, you look lifeless.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.360
Exactly!

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:24.480
We dress how we want to
and say what we want to here.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.360
Not like outside.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:34.080
Being a woman is really hard!
They constantly belittle us.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:39.760
Lots of women would prefer to not be a woman
and to live in a man's body.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:46.280
The courage of Gina's generation amazes Mahjan,

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:47.640
who owns the salon.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.800
At 40 years old,

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.920
she always wears the hijab outside.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:00.000
My generation were also against it,

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:06.800
but we had no choice
because our parents forced us.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:13.840
This generation is supported by my own.
So, it's easier for them to protest.

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.960
Gina's day-to-day life is similar to millions of Iranian women.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.280
She's married and mothered to a little three-year-old boy,

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:23.040
Sorosh.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.320
It's Poo, the bee.

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:35.160
Over time the young woman has learned to play by the Islamic rules.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:36.600
For her clothes,

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.720
her wardrobe is divided into two.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:49.600
Sadly, I've got two types of clothes.
Religious outfits like this one.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.960
And in another wardrobe...

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:03.520
These are the outfits I wear around the house
or when I'm invited to a party.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.760
I would like to only wear dresses like this one.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:16.480
Like all women and girls around the world
Iwould like to dress like that to go out.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.840
Not in the clothes they make me wear.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.480
It's a horrible feeling.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.440
Her husband condemns a regime that wants to control everything,

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.400
even when it means hiding the reality of the country.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.840
The news channels aren't credible.
You can't believe what they say.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:43.600
You can't trust them.
Nothing is reliable with this government.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:51.480
It's impossible for young people to speak about their wish for freedom in the media.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:53.600
So in recent months...

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.200
Once night falls,

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:59.360
Iranians like Gina have taken to shouting their anger from their windows.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:04.160
Death to the government
that's killing our children!

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:06.640
Down with the dictatorship!

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:12.960
It's an easy form of resistance,
like taking off the hijab.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:16.120
And

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.040
these Iranians don't hesitate to lash out directly at the head of the regime.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:26.440
Like many Iranians,

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:31.600
Jina condemns a theocratic regime that is capable of murder if it means staying in power.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:41.520
The faces of religious leaders are everywhere on the streets of the capital city Tehran.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:46.440
Huge posters remind people of passages from the Quran.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.400
The mullahs have been imposing Islamic law,

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:50.840
or Sharia law,

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:53.640
on the whole society for the past 44 years.

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.800
But many Iranians are doing everything they can to escape it.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:02.480
Maryam,

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:04.840
who also refuses to wear the hijab,

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:10.280
wants to show us this new rebellious Tehran that infuriates the mullahs.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.240
Hello! How much is this?

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.080
480,000 tomans

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.120
On a city centre street,

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:20.440
lingerie shops,

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.320
which were once hidden from public view,

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.640
now have shop displays that are considered risky.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:31.120
Before, they hid the display behind fabric, but
they've taken it away, which I find interesting.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:38.280
The conservative authorities even seem to have lost ground in the rich neighborhoods of northern Tehran.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.840
In this ultra-modern shopping centre,

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.920
it almost seems like you're in Paris or New York.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.680
Mariam can buy all Western fashion has to offer.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:57.520
Jewellery,

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:00.920
luxury watches and even dresses by leading brands.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:08.320
I'm in the Palladium shopping centre.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:18.480
You can find products here
that don't exist anywhere else in Tehran.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.680
To the great despair of religious leaders,

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:25.080
couples even walk hand in hand here,

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.240
and it's rare to see a girl in a hijab.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:34.560
Most women wear the hijab
in a really free and relaxed way

00:12:34.720 --> 00:12:38.880
compared to other places in Tehran.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.760
Clothing fashion has changed.
It's not that the regime has accepted it.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.600
It's not that the regime made this change.

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.240
It's women who have pulled back their rights
a tiny bit at a time.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:53.440
In Islamic republic propaganda,
their idol is having women at home.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.920
Women can't work without the agreement
of their husband

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:04.240
Women can't leave their house
if their husband doesn't agree.

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:10.880
A woman's life is worth half the life of a man.
That's in-the penal code.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:18.720
This archaic vision of women's place in society is highlighted in the Mullahs'

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:20.800
propaganda on state television channels.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:26.840
In this footage from February 2023,

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:27.520
Ali Khamenei,

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.640
who is the highest religious authority in Iran and aged 84,

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:37.200
takes center stage surrounded by hundreds of little girls who are covered from head to toe.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:42.160
Mothers and daughters are all soldiers.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:47.520
This is Iran.
Look at my country!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.240
According to the supreme leader,

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.800
those who don't want to conform to Islamic law are enemies.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:57.680
We will not allow this,

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:03.840
the government of the Islamic Republic
will settle the score with these criminals.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:08.960
God is great!
God is great!

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:12.400
Khamenei is our guide!
Long live the Islamic revolution.

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.040
clip produced by the authorities,

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.040
Madam, one moment!

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:19.360
Do not enter.
Put your hijab on.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:25.040
A security officer asks women to cover themselves before being able to enter the underground.

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:27.840
Do it and then you'll be able to go in.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:31.200
Thank you.

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:38.560
There's a deep dichotomy between Iranian society.
which is one of the most liberal in the world,

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.480
and the regime,
which is one of the most backwards.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.280
As well as oppressing women,

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.720
the regime enforces mass censorship.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:49.880
But this is another area in which Iranians are resisting.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:52.080
Mariam,

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:54.000
our guide to rebel Tehran,

00:14:54.520 --> 00:15:00.120
has led us to a little shop or a bookstore that is disobeying the Muller's orders.

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:01.720
In theory,

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:03.320
Western music is prohibited,

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:07.480
but here you can get your hands on records by the biggest international stars,

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.440
like the Village People and the Beatles.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.360
And under a pile of books,

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:19.800
amazing souvenirs from an era when religious leaders weren't in power.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.360
At that time, big musicians gave concerts in Iran.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:26.720
Like Frank Sinatra.
Or Enrico Macias.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.520
That was from a charity concert.

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:35.400
The music of Iran is the result

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.080
of the

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:43.520
We can't release anything
that's considered anti-religious.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:50.320
So, books that mention sex, drugs or alcohol.
They have a problem with that.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.440
Rules that infuriate Maryam.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:03.120
We live in the same country but there's a really
big disconnect between the people on one side

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:07.040
and the leaders of the regime on the other.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:10.880
The gap is huge.

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:17.280
It seems like we live in a parallel universe.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:27.160
This young woman,

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:31.440
who works somewhere in Tehran as part of the regime censorship process,

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.920
has agreed to show us their radical methods.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:36.320
The risk is exceptional.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:44.720
Lots of Hollywood blockbusters have passed through her hands,

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:48.120
including one of the biggest successes in the history of cinema,

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:49.280
Titanic.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:57.360
For a censor Titanio is a relatively easy film.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:04.160
Their clothes are quite appropriate,
apart from in a few scenes.

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:15.600
It's a really important scene, the drawing scene.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:20.720
You mustn't be able to see the folds of the breasts
and, even if it's not visible

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:24.960
the women's neckline must not be too low-cut.

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.120
I'm going to try and zoom in.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:30.880
All the shots of the heroine undergo the same treatment.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.080
They're re-framed to make her chest disappear.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:39.680
The shoulders can be visible.
as long as we can't see the fold of the underarms.

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:45.640
But sometimes a scene is too revealing and zooming in won't suffice.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:50.520
We must delete this part.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:58.960
It's cut the scene down a lot but that's the way it is.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.840
You know, in Iran, there are no uncensored films.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:07.280
I'm sacrificing myself
by watching them before release.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:12.560
I'm going to hell so that others can go to paradise.
That's just the way it is.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:19.200
These ultra-purist rules infiltrating the everyday life of Iranians have not always existed.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:23.880
At the start of the

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.960
1970s, the streets of Tehran looked like this.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.000
Women wore skirts and the hijab was a rare sight.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:31.240
At that time,

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:32.480
Iran was a monarchy.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:33.600
Their king,

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:34.240
the Shah,

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:36.360
Mohammed Reza Pahlavi,

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:38.400
wanted to westernize his country.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.240
Azadeh Kian is Iranian.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:53.600
No one came up to you on the street
to ask you what you were wearing,

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:57.520
who you were going out with or walking with, etc.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:02.000
When I tell my son now that when I was 15

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:07.920
we went dancing in discos that were reserved
for young people my age to go after school,

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.520
he doesn't believe me.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:18.480
He suppressed any opposition and monopolized all wealth,

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:22.200
while most of the Iranian people lived in great poverty.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:24.200
In 1978,

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.400
at the end of their tether,

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:29.800
the people rose up and demanded an end to the Shah's dictatorship.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:41.040
Death to the Shah!
Death to the Shah!

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:42.880
In the aftermath,

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.640
one face kept appearing,

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.840
that of a Shiite religious leader,

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.400
the Ayatollah Khomeini.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:49.600
At that time,

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:51.280
he was a refugee in France,

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:52.800
in the small village of

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:54.040
Yvelins, Neuf.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:54.800
Fleur Le Chateau.

00:19:55.560 --> 00:19:57.800
By his side was Mohsen Sassegare,

00:19:58.240 --> 00:19:59.600
a young militant Islamist.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:06.240
I was only

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:12.160
22 years old and very impressive for me that a

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:18.880
78-year-old clergy who was at the focal point of most of the news of the world.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.720
and the leadership of a revolution.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:29.680
Journalists from around the world rushed to film this man as he prepared to overthrow the Shah.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:33.680
The press even described him as a freedom fighter.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:40.880
Ayatollah Khomeini could subject the creation
of the Islamic Republic to a popular vote.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:44.560
A Republic that will guarantee
all freedoms of expression,

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:48.320
thought, worship or ideology, even Marxist.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:50.920
These promises were never kept.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:53.680
At the start of 1979,

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:54.800
under popular pressure,

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:59.800
the Shah relinquished power and the Ayatollah returned to Tehran as a hero.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.160
Then he founded the first Islamic Republic in the world,

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:14.200
with a parliament and a president,

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:16.040
just like any democracy.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:17.840
But in reality,

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:23.000
Ayatollah Khomeini seized all power and established a religious dictatorship.

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:31.120
He became the Supreme Leader, that is to say
he was absolute power personified.

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:32.960
The Supreme Leader is the real president.

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.440
The Supreme Leader is the commander-in-chief
of the armed forces.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.600
The Supreme Leader is the person
who is named for life.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.560
His first followers,

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.320
including Mohsen Sassegara,

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.440
felt betrayed.

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:50.000
Make heaven and the earth,

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.840
a spiritual regime,

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:55.080
a new way in politics.

00:21:57.320 --> 00:22:01.200
We didn't know that such a way would take the way.

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:04.400
We realised he'd lied to us.

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:10.400
We realised there would be a regression
in terms of women's rights.

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:15.600
For example, the legal age of marriage for girls
was 18 years old under the Shah

00:22:15.760 --> 00:22:19.760
but it was brought back to 9 years old
under the Islamic regime.

00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:24.760
The world was outraged and Iran withdrew from the international stage.

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:32.080
Today,

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.480
more than three out of four Iranians would like the Mullahs'

00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:36.680
dictatorship to end.

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:44.600
Since September 2022 and the murder of Masha Amini,

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.920
who was beaten to death by the Morality Police,

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:51.520
people have been attacking all symbols of the regime.

00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:54.440
Molotov cocktails thrown at mosques,

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:57.480
portraits of religious leaders burned in public,

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:02.480
propaganda posters destroyed and anti-regime tags graffitied.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:05.800
Across the country,

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:08.400
thousands of Iranians are unwavering.

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:10.800
in their defiance of the authorities.

00:23:11.440 --> 00:23:13.000
In autumn 2022,

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:18.440
high schools and universities became impassioned about the issue and took to the streets.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:22.640
The authorities feared a youth rebellion more than anything.

00:23:23.240 --> 00:23:25.200
So they ordered students to be arrested,

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:30.080
as this confidential internal memo that we have managed to obtain shows.

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:36.440
It came from the Supreme National Security Council and is addressed to the Minister of Education.

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:44.320
The disruptive constituents must be arrested outside of their educational establishments and handed over to the judicial authorities.

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:47.960
Hundreds of arrests followed.

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:54.720
What was more surprising was that thousands of schoolgirls were also victims of mysterious gas attacks.

00:23:55.400 --> 00:23:57.040
The gas used caused nausea,

00:23:57.320 --> 00:23:59.120
vomiting and breathing problems.

00:23:59.800 --> 00:24:01.920
Despite strong suspicions against them,

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:04.160
the authorities denied all involvement.

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:15.040
Very soon after,

00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:17.040
to quieten the widespread uprising,

00:24:17.360 --> 00:24:20.520
the regime decided to employ even more barbaric methods.

00:24:20.880 --> 00:24:23.480
It gave the order to open fire on protesters.

00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:32.800
Those in power used weapons of war against its own people.

00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:36.720
Lift him up!
Lift him up!

00:24:37.120 --> 00:24:38.560
Thousands of people were wounded.

00:24:38.560 --> 00:24:41.000
How did he save them?

00:24:47.440 --> 00:24:50.800
As soon as you step foot in the street in Iran
to protest,

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:56.640
to oppose the regime or even if you sing
the shortest slogan against the Supreme Leader,

00:24:56.880 --> 00:24:58.080
you risk your life.

00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:34.120
These scenes of extremely violent repression happen over and over again across the country,

00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:35.920
and leave hundreds dead.

00:25:36.640 --> 00:25:41.680
530 people dead, including around 60 children
and 38 women.

00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:45.360
They're the sort of figures that make your head spin

00:25:45.520 --> 00:25:49.360
and allow us in a way to measure
the breadth of the repression in Iran

00:25:49.520 --> 00:25:50.960
and shows what the regime is capable of.

00:25:50.960 --> 00:25:55.360
The regime defines itself
as the incarnation of Islam.

00:25:55.520 --> 00:26:03.280
Therefore, if you act against the regime, to them
that's as if you're acting against the religion itself.

00:26:07.680 --> 00:26:08.720
In only six months,

00:26:08.960 --> 00:26:11.400
at least 20,000 people were arrested.

00:26:20.520 --> 00:26:24.840
A woman who was victim to this repression after attending several protests

00:26:25.280 --> 00:26:27.000
wanted to share her experience.

00:26:27.520 --> 00:26:30.960
She dares to speak out because she has managed to flee Iran.

00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:38.880
I've decided to speak out
because the world needs to understand

00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:41.600
what's happening in the Islamic republic.

00:26:42.960 --> 00:26:48.160
Elahi is a young human rights activist who has already been imprisoned several times,

00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:51.640
notably in the dreaded Evin prison in Tehran.

00:26:51.640 --> 00:26:51.760
on.

00:26:52.640 --> 00:26:58.240
When you're imprisoned there, firstly they
interrogate you, then they put you in isolation.

00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:01.040
They give you two ruined and dirty blankets,

00:27:01.200 --> 00:27:04.880
so you put one over yourself
and use the other as a cushion.

00:27:07.280 --> 00:27:11.320
Most of the country's political and intellectual prisoners are being held at Evin.

00:27:12.280 --> 00:27:13.480
In this prison footage,

00:27:13.800 --> 00:27:16.000
